## 3. Education billing model

Education billing requires a distinction between the student, the payer, and the billing obligation.

### Core data model

| Object | Meaning | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Institution | Education provider | BrightFuture Group |
| Campus | School or branch | Jakarta Campus |
| Student | Person receiving education | Student ID |
| Guardian / payer | Person responsible for payment | Parent ID |
| Program | Education program | Primary School |
| Academic period | School year or semester | 2027/2028 |
| Fee type | Category of charge | Tuition |
| Billing obligation | Amount due for a period or event | Tuition Billing ID |
| Payment attempt | Individual collection attempt | Transaction ID |

### Recommended relationship

```text id="x1q7nb"
        EDUCATION GROUP
               |
        +------+------+
        |             |
        v             v
     CAMPUS A      CAMPUS B
        |
        v
      STUDENT
        |
        +-------------------+
        |                   |
        v                   v
     GUARDIAN            PROGRAM
        |                   |
        +---------+---------+
                  |
                  v
            FEE OBLIGATIONS
                  |
          +-------+-------+
          |               |
          v               v
       TUITION         OTHER FEES
          |               |
          +-------+-------+
                  |
                  v
              PAYMENT
```

### Important design principle

A student is not necessarily the payer.

One guardian may pay for multiple students. One student may have multiple authorized payers. The merchant's system should own the relationship and provide stable identifiers for billing and reconciliation.

Do not assume FlexiBill automatically provides a family-account or multi-student payer hierarchy. Validate the required data model and integration.

