## 6. Merchant configuration blueprint

### Step 1 — Define Collection structure

Possible structures:

| Collection | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Primary School | Primary education billing |
| Junior High School | Junior high billing |
| Senior High School | Senior high billing |
| University | Higher education billing |
| Jakarta Campus | Campus-specific billing |
| Bandung Campus | Campus-specific billing |
| Corporate Education | Sponsored or corporate-funded education |

Choose a structure that supports billing operations and reporting without creating unnecessary duplication.

### Step 2 — Define Plans

Example Plans:

- Primary School Tuition.
- Junior High Tuition.
- Senior High Tuition.
- University Semester Fee.
- Monthly Learning Program.
- Annual Education Package.
- Transportation Package.

### Step 3 — Configure Pricing

| Plan | Pricing model | Example | Frequency |
|---|---|---:|---|
| Monthly Tuition | Flat Fee | Rp2,500,000 | Monthly |
| Semester Tuition | Flat Fee | Rp8,000,000 | Per semester |
| Annual Fee | Flat Fee | Rp1,500,000 | Annual |
| Transportation | Flat Fee | Rp750,000 | Monthly |
| Examination | One-time amount | Rp500,000 | Event-based |

Validate available pricing models, billing intervals, and end conditions before implementation.

### Step 4 — Map student and payer records

Recommended mapping:

| Field | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Institution ID | Education provider |
| Campus ID | School or branch |
| Student ID | Stable student identifier |
| Guardian ID | Stable payer identity |
| Academic year | Reporting and billing period |
| Program ID | Education program |
| Fee type | Tuition or other charge |
| Billing ID | Unique fee obligation |
| Due date | Payment deadline |
| Amount due | Approved fee amount |

Use stable identifiers. Names, phone numbers, and email addresses should not be used as the only reconciliation keys.

### Step 5 — Define billing schedules

Example:

| Fee | Schedule |
|---|---|
| Registration | At enrollment |
| Tuition | Every month |
| Semester fee | At semester start |
| Annual fee | Once per academic year |
| Examination fee | Before examination |
| Transportation | Monthly |

Define:
- Billing start date.
- Billing frequency.
- Due date.
- Academic period.
- Fee amount source.
- Late-payment policy.
- Collection window.
- Payment confirmation process.

The education system should remain the source of truth for academic periods and fee calculations unless another approved architecture is established.

### Step 6 — Select the integration model

Potential approaches:

| Model | Suitable when | Validation |
|---|---|---|
| DOKU-hosted Billing Automation | Standard recurring billing can be configured in FlexiBill | Confirm workflow and data ownership |
| API / H2H | Education ERP controls billing and requires integration | Confirm required APIs and webhook events |
| Hybrid | Institution calculates fees while FlexiBill supports agreed billing and collection functions | Define system boundaries |
| Account Billing | Billing is organized around an account and calendar-date model | Validate exact use case fit |

Do not choose a model solely because it is technically available. Select it based on who owns the billing obligation and academic schedule.

