### Journey C — Parent paying for multiple children

Example:

A parent has two children enrolled in the same education group.

| Student | Billing obligation | Amount |
|---|---|---:|
| Student A | Monthly tuition | Rp2,500,000 |
| Student B | Monthly tuition | Rp2,500,000 |
| Student B | Transportation | Rp750,000 |
| **Total** | | **Rp5,750,000** |

The institution may want to present one payer-level view of several obligations.

This is a customer-experience and data-integration requirement. Do not assume that native consolidated invoicing or multi-student account aggregation is available.

Possible implementation designs:
- Separate payment requests per billing obligation.
- Merchant-generated payer summary with separate payment references.
- A consolidated payment experience where supported and validated.
- An API-driven payment journey with merchant-side allocation logic.

The institution must define whether the parent pays obligations individually or through an approved consolidated payment model.

