### Customer experience principles

- Show the student name and reference clearly.
- Identify the relevant academic year or semester.
- Explain fee type and due date.
- Show the amount due and payment status.
- Avoid ambiguous payment references.
- Explain late-payment rules.
- Provide a clear support contact.
- Protect student and guardian information.

## 9. Outstanding fees and recovery

### Typical failure scenarios

| Scenario | Recommended handling |
|---|---|
| Insufficient funds | Notify payer and follow permitted recovery rules |
| Expired payment credential | Request an eligible payment-method update |
| Bank decline | Explain next action without exposing sensitive internal details |
| Payment pending | Avoid creating duplicate payment obligations |
| Late payment | Apply institution's approved late-fee policy |
| Wrong student reference | Resolve allocation before changing payment status |
| Duplicate notification | Reconcile idempotently |
| Partial payment | Apply only if the institution's policy and integration support it |

### Operational monitoring

Track:
- Total fees due.
- Successful collections.
- Failed collections.
- Outstanding amount.
- Overdue amount.
- Recovered obligations.
- Payment success by campus.
- Collection success by payment method.
- Outstanding amount by academic period.

Do not treat a failed attempt as an unpaid fee if another valid payment has already settled the same billing obligation.

